^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] observe — The consumer filed fourteen plugin and tooling asks on 2026-10-25, seven from reading the editors and protocol and seven from using the VS Code extension on its route trees and plan notebooks. Ranks 5 and 8 had no home here: no plan owned the plugin protocol, .spw/surfaces/plugins holds only a stub index, and no runner reads the scan path.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] decide — This plan owns the first plugin and the intake table for all fourteen asks, so the consumer reads one place after each submodule update. Every other ask joins the plan that already owns its files.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] taste — The workbench owns the protocol, the runner, and the health rules; the consumer owns the plugin file. The expression manifest reads data-spw-semantic-expression, which only the consumer writes, so its plugin file belongs in the consumer and this repo tests the runner with a fixture plugin of its own.
 >>[2026-10-25 21:34] implement — Ranks 6 (the stats half), 9, 10, 11 and 12 are implemented and verified on main, uncommitted: build clean, test:lsp 389 of 390 (the one failure predates this work, logged in form-geometry-editor), test:cli 322, test:vscode 73, extension typecheck clean, poll-review clean. Each home plan holds the commit. Rank 6 stale-diagnostic half stays routed to apposition-cache-granules.
 >>[2026-10-26 12:16] implement — Landed: rank 6 stats half in 2a3dac47, rank 11 in cf7df67a, ranks 9, 10 and 12 in 55e79d2e. Nine asks stay routed and two are owned here.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:19] revise — Intake count after the 2026-10-26 landings: seven asks routed, two owned here (5 and 8), four landed whole (9, 10, 11 and 12), and rank 6 split: the stats half landed in 2a3dac47, the stale-diagnostic half stays routed to apposition-cache-granules. The 12:16 entry said nine routed. The slow_loop row now gives one status per home.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[first_plugin]: "Is the first plugin the expression manifest (proves select and emit on a corpus the consumer already builds by script, and touches its publish path) or a doctor reading of projection freshness (smaller, answers a registry that already exists, touches a view)?"
 ?[reader_name]: "Does an emit name a reader by module path or by the selector it reads? A module path fails when the module moves; a selector fails only when nothing reads the field."
 ?[verb_home]: "Does the runner live under spw emit, beside pack and fractal, or under its own spw plugin verb?"
}

